## Context

Tasks 1-3 built the `internal/known` package and added a `--known-modules-file` flag + post-success cache write to `cmd/diff.go`. The `resolveKnownPath(override string) string` helper exists in `diff.go` and is reusable.

Your job: add cobra `ValidArgsFunction` for shell tab-completion on BOTH the diff and versions subcommands. The diff subcommand already has its `--known-modules-file` flag (from Task 3); the versions subcommand needs the same flag added because it's currently flagless.

Cobra exposes a `__complete` pseudo-command that lets tests drive completion directly: `root.SetArgs([]string{"__complete", "diff", "--known-modules-file", knownFile, ""})` triggers the registered ValidArgsFunction and writes the suggestions to stdout, one per line.

Note: `birdseye versions ns/n/p` success does NOT add to the cache (intentional). Only diff and the interactive picker write. But versions DOES read the cache for completion — that's the asymmetry.

