## Notes & Style

- The cobra `__complete` pseudo-command is the official testing surface for `ValidArgsFunction`. It writes one suggestion per line followed by a `:N` directive line — `strings.Contains` is enough for test assertions.
- `cobra.ShellCompDirectiveNoFileComp` disables fallback filename completion, so users don't see local files mixed with module addresses.
- The `if len(args) > 0` guard means we only suggest module addresses for the FIRST positional arg. Subsequent args (versions) get no suggestions.
- `versions` reuses `resolveKnownPath` from `diff.go` (same package) — no need to duplicate.
- `versions.go` declares its own local `knownModulesFile` var (not on `diffOpts`) because there's no per-command opts struct for versions; that's fine and idiomatic.

## Code Organization

`diff.go` and `versions.go` each get the small `ValidArgsFunction` addition inline. No new files.

